  "reviews": [
    {
      "reviewbody": "I was at the show that night and I had no idea they were gunna jam so hard! This is definately my favorite show of all the ones i've downloaded and its not just because I was there. The sound quality is also very good for a live show.",
      "reviewtitle": "A very sick show",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "phishindavelvetc",
      "createdate": "2007-01-08 00:42:34",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-08 00:42:34"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "I am still thinking about this show to this day and its almost been a month. Just amazing. They were on fire the whole night. Jamie seems to blow my mind everytime. They jammed so hard and I've never seen Waterstreet that rockin, everyone-I mean everyone was dancing. Nick, thank you so much for the tape, the sound quality is A+. G-nome is amazing, but VL Tone and Jagoff for encore stole the show.",
      "reviewtitle": "Lost for words",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "keasy3",
      "createdate": "2007-01-08 15:05:19",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-08 15:05:19"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "I agree that the band was on fire.  Dan's bass tone is getting crunchy (yet still very clean) and is really cutting thru.  This show was one of the best I've seen.\n\nBack in '02, tND played as \"The Nude Eel,\" opening for Karl Denson's Tiny Universe at Water Street...  They played the most incredible jam between \"Homewrecker\" and \"VL Tone\" that nite -- best jam I've heard, with each member of the band doin' some awesome stuff.  You can check that nite out at:\nhttp://www.archive.org/details/tnd2002-12-16.shnf",
      "reviewtitle": "If you liked this VL Tone, dude...",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "DW",
      "createdate": "2007-01-09 04:18:05",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-09 04:18:05"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "im so happy that they put this show on archive b/c it is so good if u don't have get.",
      "reviewtitle": "this is it",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "chikin",
      "createdate": "2007-01-11 01:16:05",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-11 01:16:05"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "uhh pretty sure track 3 and track 5 of the second set are moonscraper not glide",
      "reviewtitle": "moonscraper?",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "UPStatejammster",
      "createdate": "2007-01-14 18:54:57",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-27 21:28:28"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "Set 1, track 2 is a tease/mini-cover of Futurerock's Da Funk starts for anyone who doesn't know/was wondering why it sounded familar/wants to know. Starts about 12 seconds into this track.\n\nOther than that, amazing show, incredibly tight, they keep getting better and better!",
      "reviewtitle": "A Side Note",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "DSGN",
      "createdate": "2007-01-17 16:00:11",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-17 16:00:11"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "FYI - Da Funk is a tune by Daft Punk that is covered by Future Rock.  If you don't own Daft Punk's album Home Work - then go get it...legendary.\n\nGreat recording here, nice job Nick",
      "reviewtitle": "Da Funk",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "ingsy",
      "createdate": "2007-01-17 21:11:25",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-17 21:11:25"
    },
    {
      "reviewbody": "I'm not usually a big fan of mic'd live recordings, but this turned out quite well.  I just wanted to drop a few lines and thank Nick for recording the show.  This show was the first time that I saw TND live.  I've been a soundguy for the past 10 years and have mixed a ton of bands and worked a ton of shows.  This show was probably my all time favorite.  Great band, great performance and great crowd.  As soon as I hit track two, I started bobbing my head at my desk just like I was there again.  Thank you!!!",
      "reviewtitle": "Thank you!",
      "stars": "5",
      "reviewer": "Zach Dumrese",
      "createdate": "2007-01-18 17:42:33",
      "reviewdate": "2007-01-18 17:42:33"
    }
  ]
